 {
  "verse_id": "tsa-a05-v03",
  "song": "tsa-a05",
  "verse": 3,
  "quick_english": "When the concept depends on another means for its own impression — taking mind, breath, body, pot etc. as limited-formed means, reaching subtlety, it brings forth āṇava knowledge. Therein: mind is meditation-natured; breath gross and subtle — first, articulation-natured; articulation is the five prāṇa-functions; the subtle is denoted by letter-sound, to be said later; body is arrangement-specific, denoted by instrument-sound; pots etc. external, to be praised as means by pot-pit-liṅga-worship.",
